 "_t1/github/out/sim": "### 1. 'Create repository' on the host = an empty bare repository\n$ git init --bare -q --initial-branch=main github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n\n$ ls github.com/an/ct-shop.git\nconfig\ndescription\nHEAD\nhooks\ninfo\nobjects\nrefs\n\n### 2. An: a local project with one commit, then connect it to the remote\n$ git status --short --ignored\n!! .env\n\n$ git check-ignore -v .env\n.gitignore:3:.env\t.env\n\n$ git remote add origin github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n\n$ git remote -v\norigin\tgithub.com/an/ct-shop.git (fetch)\norigin\tgithub.com/an/ct-shop.git (push)\n\n$ git push -u origin main\nTo github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n * [new branch]      main -> main\nbranch 'main' set up to track 'origin/main'.\n\n$ git status -sb\n## main...origin/main\n\n### 3. Committed is not pushed\n$ git status -sb\n## main...origin/main [ahead 1]\n\n$ git push\nTo github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n   8161c6f..6ea36d0  main -> main\n\n$ git status -sb\n## main...origin/main\n\n### 4. Binh clones the project\n$ git clone github.com/an/ct-shop.git binh\nCloning into 'binh'...\ndone.\n\n$ git log --oneline\n6ea36d0 Add home page\n8161c6f Initial commit: README and .gitignore\n\n$ git push\nTo github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n   6ea36d0..a8272b6  main -> main\n\n### 5. An, meanwhile, commits without pulling first — push is rejected\n$ git push\nTo github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n ! [rejected]        main -> main (fetch first)\nerror: failed to push some refs to 'github.com/an/ct-shop.git'\nhint: Updates were rejected because the remote contains work that you do not\nhint: have locally. This is usually caused by another repository pushing to\nhint: the same ref. If you want to integrate the remote changes, use\nhint: 'git pull' before pushing again.\nhint: See the 'Note about fast-forwards' in 'git push --help' for details.\n\n$ git pull --rebase\nFrom github.com/an/ct-shop\n   6ea36d0..a8272b6  main       -> origin/main\nRebasing (1/1)\nSuccessfully rebased and updated refs/heads/main.\n\n$ git log --oneline --graph\n* 4d21e2a Document how to run\n* a8272b6 Add shipping note\n* 6ea36d0 Add home page\n* 8161c6f Initial commit: README and .gitignore\n\n$ git push\nTo github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n   a8272b6..4d21e2a  main -> main\n\n### 6. A pull request is a branch on the remote, waiting to be merged\n$ git switch -c feature/cart\nSwitched to a new branch 'feature/cart'\n\n$ git push -u origin feature/cart\nTo github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n * [new branch]      feature/cart -> feature/cart\nbranch 'feature/cart' set up to track 'origin/feature/cart'.\n\n$ git branch -a\n* feature/cart\n  main\n  remotes/origin/HEAD -> origin/main\n  remotes/origin/feature/cart\n  remotes/origin/main\n\n$ git ls-remote --heads origin\n12c727d9c69294252e0e45a69990f1d54ae96f0c\trefs/heads/feature/cart\n4d21e2a00d865d078c3989a1a4d1e558879a211d\trefs/heads/main\n\n### 7. Merging the pull request = a merge commit on main, pushed by the host\n$ git switch main\nSwitched to branch 'main'\nYour branch is up to date with 'origin/main'.\n\n$ git merge --no-ff feature/cart -m \"Merge pull request #1 from an/feature/cart\"\nMerge made by the 'ort' strategy.\n index.html | 1 +\n 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)\n\n$ git push\nTo github.com/an/ct-shop.git\n   4d21e2a..31ceb3a  main -> main\n\n$ git log --oneline --graph\n*   31ceb3a Merge pull request #1 from an/feature/cart\n|\\  \n| * 12c727d Add cart button\n|/  \n* 4d21e2a Document how to run\n* a8272b6 Add shipping note\n* 6ea36d0 Add home page\n* 8161c6f Initial commit: README and .gitignore",
